1. All game logic should always be in operations.py, not qt_networked.py
2. In qt_networked.py, the PC version and networked version should use the same code. (There should be very little branching between versions.)
3. There should never be redundant code.
4. Tests should always be written as unit tests in seperate files from the main code.
5. There should be no need to update qt.py in the future, as it should not be used because the code uses the qt_networked.py code.
6. The user should be able to create new OSM maps without modifying any current files
7. Do not create new unit test files. Use preexisting ones.
8. Core files (operations.py, map.py, game.py, ai.py, map_preset_loader.py) must not contain hardcoded references to specific map presets (e.g. nyc, ny_metro). Use map_preset_loader, preset discovery, and preset-provided functions. Map-specific logic belongs in map_presets_*.py files.
9. AI thinking logic can be in ai.py instead of operations.py